# Supply-chain cooldown.
#
# A compromised release is usually unpublished or patched within hours; refusing to install
# anything younger than this removes the day-zero window for both `npm install` here and
# `npm ci` in CI. The exposure is the transitive closure in package-lock.json — several
# hundred packages — not the three dozen declared in package.json.
#
# If a genuine same-day security patch is ever blocked, npm keeps the older version, WARNS,
# and exits non-zero — so it fails loudly rather than silently doing the wrong thing. To
# take an urgent fix: `npm install --min-release-age=0 <pkg>`, then restore this file.
#
# This applies to *resolution*, so `npm ci` replaying an existing lockfile is unaffected.
min-release-age=3
